WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
Oh, good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday. As you might notice, I'm here in my new office

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.480
and I'm walking on my treadmill desk

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.540
Why did I get a treadmill desk? Well, two reasons, Hank

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:13.420
First, I am a nerd and I heard that you could level up in your nerdiness by getting a treadmill desk

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.600
So I was like, 'alright'

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.560
To talk about the second reason, we need to go back in time to Memorial Day weekend

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.340
when you and I went to the beach together

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.080
Now Hank, you may remember that we ran into the ocean, both wearing our shirts

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.820
to protect the public, and then we had an old-fashioned noodle war

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.540
you know, like people in their thirties do

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.660
and in that noodle war, it was widely reported that you won

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.140
but in fact, you did not win, because as you can see right here, you abandoned your noodle

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.360
which is losing! Anybody who abandons their noodle has lost the noodle war!

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.340
That's the rules!

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.400
So just to be perfectly clear, I won the noodle war

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.500
However, after I won the noodle war, you picked me up and slammed me into the water

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.040
and at some point when you were lifting this nearly 200 pound mass and then slamming it into the water,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.400
I thought to myself, 'Hank has gotten kind of fit lately'

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.840
And Hank, it turns out that over the last several months, you've quietly been doing this exercise regimen

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.480
that has resulted in you becoming kind of buff

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.760
In fact, several people commented about it on your last video

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.620
Now, I didn't get this treadmill desk just because you got fit and I'm jealous

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.820
But I'm not gonna deny it Hank, I was partly inspired by my Memorial Day dunking.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.840
Also, third reason: Hank, as you know, I am obsessed in all the ways that in trying to save ourselves we kill ourselves,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.900
Like all the the ways we act irrationally about health.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:24.620
For instance, I'm a big fan of hand sanitizer, but sometimes I use hand sanitizer while I'm driving.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.240
And that's not rational, because I'm creating more risks for myself by using the hand sanitizer than I would if I just drove.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:38.420
Anyway, Hank, it turns out that people that sit more than eleven hours a day are twice as likely to die from all causes over the next 15 years than people that sit for less than four hours a day.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.720
Well, Hank, I don't need to tell you why this is a concern to me.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.020
I live on the internet, the world capital of sitting.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.620
Initially, I thought it might not be a problem because I usually don't sit...

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.720
... I recline.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.560
But it turns out reclining count as sitting.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.320
Sitting too much increase your risks of like heart attack, diabetes, certain types of cancer...

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.760
So I was like, I'm not gonna do it anymore Hank, I'm gonna be a stander!

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.260
I'm gonna be a stander and a walker!

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.180
My entire new novel is gonna be written while walking.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.060
Or this will end up like all the other fitness crap in my basement.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.820
Hank, DFTBA, congratulations on your new found... you know.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.260
I'll see you on Friday.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.580
Alright Hank, I'm happy, so I'm gonna try this.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.120
Don't try this at home.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.480
YESSS!

